  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transformative and Integrative Build Out for All &#xa0;(TIBA)&#xa0;is the&#xa0;Young activists&#xa0;a non-profit organisation, as a community-based organisation in 2015&#x2013;16 with the goal of transforming communities via long-term initiatives that will empower and improve the lives of women, children, and youth. Later, in 2018, it was authorized to operate as a non-governmental organization in Tanzania by the NGO Act. At TIBA, everyone is treated equally and without prejudice regardless of gender, color, or ethnicity. This belief in equality and inclusion is reflected in every aspect of team selection, policy formulation, program/project design, and implementation. The future that TIBA envisions is one in which every woman, child, and young person has the same chances and aspirations and may realize their full potential in every sphere of life. To do this, TIBA seeks to develop young, women, and children who are capable of positively influencing Tanzania&apos;s growth and who are socially and economically autonomous. TIBA employs 5primary core values, including Integrity: Members of TIBA and the secretariat will operate with integrity in all of our dealings; we will be open, honest, and transparent. Cooperation across Borders: In order to reach more people at the grassroots level,TIBA will expand its services, connections, and working relationships. Gender Equity and Fairness: TIBA will work to make sure that gender considerations are incorporated into every one of our interventions, and we&apos;ll work with our partners to help them realize how crucial it is to do the same. Transparency and accountability: TIBA will be open, honest, and transparent, and we will be accountable to the people we serve for our activities.Professionalism: We will always uphold a culture of civility, respect, and professionalism. since being registered Although TIBA has greatly improved the community, its most significant achievements include TIBA has been acknowledged as a model organization in the SADC gender awards for 2019 for its work in involving men and boys as change agents. Women&apos;s Participation in Peace and Security Project Learning Presentation, Voice of Change Category, 2021, where the methodology was used as a best practice, Additionally, the Kijiwe Cha Kahawa Model has been acknowledged by theMenengage Tanzania Network as the finest strategy. Additionally, Kijiwe cha Kahawa, a community engagement initiative, has been acknowledged as a best practice program in accountability for the changes it producedat the community level. Tandale, whereKijiwe cha Kahawa TIBA enabled citizens to present on the Teenage Pregnancy Challenge broughton by a lack of Secondary School. and as a result, a secondary school construction proposal was approved by the government. In addition, Digital media&apos;s influence Afew of the accomplishments that TIBA is proud of include founding membership in the most active networks, including the Sexual Reproductive Health Alliance Tanzania Chapter and the Gender and Climate Change Tanzania Network. TIBA was recognized as aninnovative NGO for using digital media to promote the Covid19 vaccination in Tanzania.</narrative>
